;
SHUTDOWN, BACKUP AND UPDATES

A - Backups, shutdown and recovery
B - Keeping up with new releases

:A
BACKUPS, SHUTDOWN AND RECOVERY

BYE logs off a caller; it does not stop the machine. Between calls, use local
Ctrl-C at BYE's waiting prompt, then RETURN for ordinary CP/M. From private
local CP/M enter:

    SYSUTLS:BYEBYE

Wait until cpmsim has actually stopped. A blanked caller or an idle listener
is not a stopped emulator.

Copy the whole installation to separate storage: disks/, the library catalog,
uploads/inbox/, state/, RCPM.CONF and private SYSOP.DOC. In Docker, preserve
the complete persistent volume while the board is stopped. A copy on the same
disk is useful for recovery from mistakes, but not a substitute for a backup
on separate storage.

Restore a complete snapshot into a new directory. Don't mix accounts and
message files from unrelated dates. Stop the original before starting a
restored copy on its port. Never bypass the installation lock or delete it to
start a second guest on the same disks.

If WORK cleanup fails, the machine refuses to answer. Stop and repair the I:
image or host write permissions before restarting.

:B
KEEPING UP WITH NEW RELEASES

Don't unpack a new release over your board. Test it separately and follow its
migration instructions. Preserve your accounts, messages, policy, credentials,
uploads and custom software. Keep matching emulator and BYE driver versions
together. Pulling a new Docker image doesn't automatically migrate an
initialized volume.

CPMNet is not part of released 1.2.2; this guide describes local forums and
mail only. Preserve the original component and archive notices when
redistributing material. See the distribution review.
